out":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{W}{W}","name":"Silver Knight","oracle_id":"aa7cd6e6-35a6-4c18-9d66-dc2a95206401","oracle_text":"First strike, protection from red","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2011-04-01","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature — Human Knight"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":["B"],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Swamp","oracle_id":"56719f6a-1a6c-4c0a-8d21-18f7d7350b68","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {B}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["B"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land — Swamp"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If Lignify leaves the battlefield, the creature goes back to being what it was before. Any effects that applied while the Lignify was on the battlefield, such as Giant Growth or Lace with Moonglove, will continue to apply.","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2007-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a previous effect switched the creature's power and toughness, that effect still applies (though it will apply to the creature's new power and toughness).","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2007-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the enchanted creature has a characteristic-defining ability that specifies its color, that ability will still have its effect because it's applied before the creature loses the ability.","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2007-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Lignify causes the enchanted creature to lose all abilities it had at the time it became enchanted. Any abilities granted to the creature after Lignify entered the battlefield will work normally.","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2007-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Lignify overwrites characteristic-defining abilities that specify the enchanted creature's power or toughness (such as the one Dauntless Dourbark has) or that specify its creature types (such as changeling does).","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2007-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Lignify overwrites previous effects that changed the enchanted creature's creature types. Any such effects that apply after Lignify enters will work normally.","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2007-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Lignify will overwrite static abilities that come from the creature itself (such as the one on Verduran Enchantress) because Lignify causes the creature to lose that ability before it gets a chance to apply.","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2007-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Lignify will not overwrite effects such as those from Glorious Anthem, counters, or Giant Growth that change the enchanted creature's power or toughness without setting it to a specific value. Apply such effects after applying Lignify.","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Lignify will overwrite any previous effects that set the enchanted creature's power or toughness (such as Serendib Sorcerer does). Any such effects that apply after Lignify entered will work normally.","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Kindred is a card type that allows noncreature cards to have creature types. For example, Echoes of Eternity is an Eldrazi (although not a creature) while on the battlefield and an Eldrazi card (although not a creature card) in zones other than the battlefield.","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This cards was originally printed with the \"tribal\" card type. That card type has been replaced with \"kindred\". This change does not affect the gameplay function of this card.","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While it appears only on cards that already have other card types, kindred is a card type and will be counted by effects that refer to the number of card types among cards in a zone.","oracle_id":"63625b26-3a19-4c3c-b18a-91247bb2a40c","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If there are fewer than twenty cards in the targeted player's library, that player puts all the cards from their library into their graveyard.","oracle_id":"cc2b6e58-2d6f-495e-95f3-9496105c4cba","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
